<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Application 2</title>

  <style>
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Arial, sans-serif;
      background: radial-gradient(circle at top left, #0f172a, #020617);
      color: #e5e7eb;
    }

    .container {
      max-width: 960px;
      padding: 60px 40px;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: 2.6rem;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
      color: #60a5fa;
    }

    p {
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
      max-width: 720px;
    }

    .image-card {
      margin: 40px 0 20px;
      max-width: 520px;
      border-radius: 16px;
      overflow: hidden;
      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
    }

    .image-card img {
      width: 100%;
      display: block;
    }

    .badge {
      display: inline-block;
      margin-top: 20px;
      padding: 10px 18px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      border: 1px solid #60a5fa;
      color: #93c5fd;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
    }

    .card {
      margin-top: 30px;
      padding: 20px;
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
      border-radius: 14px;
      max-width: 720px;
    }

    .footer {
      margin-top: 60px;
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: #9ca3af;
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>
  <div class="container">

    <h1>Application 2</h1>

    <p>
      This page is served by <strong>Application Backend B</strong>, deployed and
      managed using <strong>Ansible</strong> as part of Week 6 of my 12-week
      technical depth programme.
    </p>

    <p>
      All application content, directory structure and permissions are enforced
      declaratively via Ansible roles — allowing safe, repeatable and idempotent
      configuration without manual server changes.
    </p>

    <p>
      Traffic reaching <code>/app2</code> is routed by the AWS Application Load
      Balancer using path-based listener rules, cleanly separating infrastructure
      provisioning (Terraform) from configuration management (Ansible).
    </p>

    <div class="image-card">
      <img src="app2.jpg" alt="Application 2 backend image">
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <strong>Served from:</strong> /app2/index.html<br>
      <strong>Managed by:</strong> Ansible role<br>
      <strong>Execution model:</strong> Idempotent configuration
    </div>

    <div class="badge">
      ALB • HTTPS • Target Group B • Ansible Managed
    </div>

    <div class="footer">
      Eirini – Technical Depth Programme • Week 6: Configuration Management
    </div>

  </div>
</body>
</html>
